# Legion Go 2 gyro (IMU udev)

Root cause: stock SteamOS udev writes `imu_bypass_enable` (missing `d`) and never sets `imu_enabled`. Controller gyros stay off. InputPlumber then has no usable handle IMU; it also filters screen IIO gyro when `hid_lenovo_go` is loaded.

Fix: `/etc/udev/rules.d/99-legion-go2-imu-fix.rules` via `fix-legion-go2-gyro.sh`. Verify both handles `imu_enabled=true` and `imu_bypass_enabled=true`. Targets should be `deck-uhid` from steamos-manager.

Never reintroduce `GYRO_GAIN=50` or custom InputPlumber overrides for this issue.
